It is five minutes to six.
I open the door.
Inside the shop it is warm and dark.
There are large sacks everywhere.
I greet the man behind the counter.
He says kindly: "Good evening."
I ask: "Which coffee can you recommend?"
He shows me two kinds of coffee.
I smell the beans.
I say: "I will take the dark coffee, please."
The man weighs out the beans.
"That makes twelve Euro," he says.
I pay.
I pack the packet into my backpack.
Then I go outside.
The sun shines on the water.
I walk a little along the river.
Now I do not have to hurry anymore.
Later I ride back with the S-Bahn.
